    {
      "id": 17,
      "plugin": "Core",
      "model": "Notes",
      "version": "2.6.6",
      "params": [],
      "pos": [
        21,
        2
      ],
      "data": {
        "text": "HEMIOLA AUDIO: WHOA!  HYPNOTIC TECHNO, 130 BPM\n\nCycle Clock (4/4) is the master. BEAT gate = kick and Whoa ACCENT. SECTION trigger resets the SEQ3 each bar so the loop never drifts.\nR&T divides the beat into eighths. That clock drives the SEQ3 (eight steps, one repeated riff) and the hats.\nWhoa! plays ratio 3 as a short FM pluck: sustain at zero, the release knobs set the note length. Slow LFOs sweep MOD D and INDEX, so the same riff keeps changing.\nDelay: dotted eighth from the BEAT clock. Reverb: small Room.\n\nKick and hat are Fundamental modules going straight to the Mixer. Not yet heard in Rack when written."
      }
    }
  ],
